Option 2: SSH (recommended for long-term)
Generate an SSH key (if you don't have one):

ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C "rahulkd.das@gmail.com"
Copy the public key:

cat ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub
Add it to GitHub → Settings → SSH and GPG keys
Switch your remote to SSH:

git remote set-url origin git@github.com:rahulkd/Production-RAG.git
Push:

git push origin RAG_infrastrcuture_setup
SSH is the better long-term setup — no tokens to rotate. The PAT approach is faster if you just want to push now.

